Teach libtiff's bundled `config.sub` about Apple's iOS-simulator host triplet.

`build.sh` configures libtiff with `--host=$HOST_TRIPLET`, and forge builds
three iOS slices: `arm64-apple-ios` (device), `arm64-apple-ios-simulator` and
`x86_64-apple-ios-simulator`. autoconf canonicalises the `--host` value through
`config/config.sub` before anything is compiled. For the simulator name that
script produces machine `<cpu>-apple` and OS `ios-simulator`, then splits the
OS on its dash into kernel `ios` and OS `simulator`. The bare word `simulator`
gets past the recognised-OS list only by accident -- it matches the unrelated
`sim*` entry meant for bare-metal simulator targets -- and then reaches the
block that validates the kernel/OS combination, which has no case for `ios` +
`simulator` and falls through to its catch-all:

    Invalid configuration 'arm64-apple-ios-simulator': Kernel 'ios' not known
    to work with OS 'simulator'.

configure stops there, so nothing is compiled and the log carries no compiler
error to chase. `arm64-apple-ios` and all the Android triplets canonicalise
cleanly; only the two simulator slices die.

libtiff 4.7.0 ships a newer config.sub (2024-05-27) than most of the other
flet-lib* recipes, which is why this patch looks slightly different from its
siblings: that vintage carries a third "object file format" component, so the
validating switch is `case $kernel-$os-$obj in` rather than `case $kernel-$os
in`. The added case is therefore `ios-simulator*-)` -- kernel `ios`, OS
`simulator`, empty `$obj` -- placed just ahead of the `*-*-*)` catch-all that
would otherwise reject it. It accepts the pairing and normalises nothing, so
`arm64-apple-ios-simulator` canonicalises to `aarch64-apple-ios-simulator` and
every other triplet behaves exactly as before.

Without it, two of the three iOS slices of flet-libtiff fail at configure, and
flet-libproj -- which requires flet-libtiff -- and everything downstream of it
(flet-libgdal, pyproj) lose their iOS wheels.

The commit that introduced this file (ec8d184, a bulk branch consolidation)
records no rationale; the account above is reconstructed from the diff and
confirmed by running libtiff's own config.sub against forge's triplets, patched
and unpatched.

diff --git a/config/config.sub b/config/config.sub
index 4aaae46..1692095 100755
--- a/config/config.sub
+++ b/config/config.sub
@@ -2259,6 +2259,8 @@ case $kernel-$os-$obj in
 	--*)
 		# Blank kernel and OS with real machine code file format is always fine.
 		;;
+	ios-simulator*-)
+		;;
 	*-*-*)
 		echo "Invalid configuration '$1': Kernel '$kernel' not known to work with OS '$os'." 1>&2
 		exit 1
